<div class="wp-block-group ifm-panel ifm-takeaways"><!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Key points</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list {"className":"ifm-ticks"} -->
<ul class="wp-block-list ifm-ticks"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Google Ads reaches people who are already searching for what you sell.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Facebook and Instagram ads reach people who were not looking, by area and interest.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Urgent and searched-for services usually suit Google. Visual and impulse buys usually suit Facebook and Instagram.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Whichever you choose, set up tracking first and start small.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list --></div>
<!-- /wp:group -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Small businesses often ask which advertising platform is better. Neither is. They work in different ways and suit different kinds of purchase. The useful question is how your customers buy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How Google Ads works</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You choose search terms, and your advert appears when someone types them into Google. You pay when they click. The strength is intent: a person searching "emergency locksmith near me" wants one now. The weakness is that you can only reach people who are already searching, and popular search terms can be expensive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How Facebook and Instagram ads work</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You choose an audience by location, age and interests, and your advert appears in their feed, stories or reels. Nobody asked to see it, so it has to catch the eye. The strength is reach: you can put a new product or offer in front of people who have never heard of you. The weakness is that most of them are not ready to buy today.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Which suits your business</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>People need you urgently</strong> (plumber, locksmith, vet): Google Ads.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>People research before buying</strong> (solicitor, builder, accountant): Google Ads, with a page that answers their questions.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>People buy when they see it</strong> (food, fashion, gifts, beauty): Facebook and Instagram.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>Something new that nobody searches for yet:</strong> Facebook and Instagram.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>A local event or offer with a deadline:</strong> Facebook and Instagram, targeted by area.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li><strong>You sell to other businesses:</strong> Google Ads first.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

